Repair the proofs of the nine standard-library declarations that did not verify with Z3 5.1.0 (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/340): `DivMod.LemmaHoistOverDenominator`, `LittleEndianNat.ToNatLeft`, `Mul.LemmaMulOrderingAuto`, `Power2.Lemma2To64`, `Seq.SortedUnique`, the two `MaxOrdinal` lemmas of `Termination`, `UnicodeEncodingForm.PartitionCodeUnitSequenceChecked` and `UnicodeStringsWithUnicodeChar.CharIsUnicodeScalarValue`. No existing statement, option or resource limit changes. New helper lemmas: `Seq.SortedUniqueHead`, `Seq.LemmaSortedByTail` and `TerminationMetric.MaxOrdinalAttained`. The proof of `CharIsUnicodeScalarValue` moves unchanged into a new module, `Std.Unicode.CharAsBv24`, which uses `{:z3ArithmeticSolver 6}`. The library's binary is rebuilt from the current sources and verified with Z3 5.1.0.
